                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] 9/10[/h1]\n[h2]General thoughts:[/h2]\nI got this game in Beta. I have played it for years. It's been my most played game on steam since it's release. It's a wonderful tactical deck builkder game, and still the best one in it's genre. The mechanics are good, the art is amazing, the music is wonderful and the puzzles are creative and really fun. the game runs well and feels really smooth. I do feel lately it has suffered from a reduced playercount. The players that are still active are really dedicated, but therefore over all also highly skilled. The threshold for new players to get into the multiplayer part of the game is high, and can be frustrating. The world bosses mechanics are really fun, but so specific it can feel demoralizing to try and figure it out without a guide. Personally I'm a fan of the draft mode and spend most of my time playing that.\n\n[h2]Pro's:[/h2]\n[list]\n[*] Great art\n[*] Great music\n[*] Runs well\n[*] Fun gamemodes with a good amount of variety\n[*] Comes with a co-op mode\n[*] Really interesting mechanics and gameplay\n[*] Dedicated playerbase\n[*] Supports a variety of tactics that are viable\n[*] All basic cards obtainable relativly fast for new players\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Con's[/h2]\n[list]\n[*] Seems to no longer be updated\n[*] Small playerbase\n[*] Achievements locked behind DLC\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Other info:[/h2]\n[b]Playtime:[/b] Infinite\n[b]Difficulty:[/b] From relativly straightforward to ''I really need a guide for this''\n[b]Achievement difficulty:[/b] Easily ofer a couple 100 hours while activly hunting for them\n[b]Replayability:[/b] For the puzzles, bosses and co-op not so much, for the rest infinite",
